I'm now going through the code again, focusing on `sendMessage` calls. I had earlier missed that I needed to pass in a dictionary. I'll search for all instances of `sendMessage` and make sure they use the correct `message` key for the argument.

I've now updated all the `sendMessage` calls to pass an object with a `message` key. This fix should correct the underlying issue. The code looks right now.


